254,448,264,6602,279,663,404,45387,11,1128,1899,315,279,2003,374,279,1156,1899,315,279,1852,2254,30,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nIn any month with a Friday the Thirteenth, what day of the week is the first day of the same month?","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"02b8bb4566164eebd39ad56527bde13bfa48148f8164264056382454899768e0"},"seconds":5.5160582065582275,"seed":945292959902379265,"stop":"eos","text":"To determine the day of the week for the first day of a month that has a Friday the Thirteenth, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. **Identify the date of the Thirteenth**: We know that the Thirteenth is a Friday.\n\n2. **Work backwards to find the first day of the month**:\n   - If the Thirteenth is a Friday, then the Twelfth is a Thursday.\n   - The Eleventh is a Wednesday.\n   - The Tenth is a Tuesday.\n   - The Ninth is a Monday.\n   - The Eighth is a Sunday.\n   - The Seventh is a Saturday.\n   - The Sixth is a Friday.\n   - The Fifth is a Thursday.\n   - The Fourth is a Wednesday.\n   - The Third is a Tuesday.\n   - The Second is a Monday.\n   - The first day of the month is a Sunday.\n\nSo, if a month has a Friday the Thirteenth, the first day of that month is a Sunday. Therefore, the answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{Sunday}}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{\\text{Sunday}}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"number_theory:115"}
